{"availability":"available","full":"crs48/wealthglobe","name":"wealthglobe","description":"If Earth's land were divided in proportion to personal net worth, how much ground would one person stand on? A 3D globe thought experiment.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-09T23:12:14Z","updated":"2026-10-10T14:39:01Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://crs48.github.io/wealthglobe/","topics":[],"demo":"https://crs48.github.io/wealthglobe/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:16.775Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:16.775Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:16.775Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T15:06:16.775Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["If every square meter of Earth's land were divided in proportion to personal net worth, how much ground would one person stand on?","A static, single-page data-visual essay on a spinning 3D globe. Click a country, a curated life, or a named fortune and see the plot of land that person would hold. The contrast is the product: Elon Musk's plot is the size of the United Kingdom; the median adult in Haiti would stand on about 60 m².","It covers the entire globe. Every country in the Natural Earth 110m polygon set has at least a mean figure, and every country with a published median has that too. Sub-Saharan Africa is the first group in the Places list, not the last."],"features":["Globe (full viewport): night texture, thin atmosphere, Natural Earth 110m country polygons colored on a log scale by mean wealth, median wealth, or either one's land claim. Hover for a tooltip with mean, median, adults,…","Claim circle: a geodesic polygon extruded slightly above the surface with a soft pulsing ring. Claims under 1 km² get a pin instead of a microscopic circle, plus a magnified inset that draws the plot to scale against a…","Top chrome: title, thesis, the metric toggle (Typical person = median, Average p